GX shaders: make the vertex position invariant.

Games draw overlays on exactly the same vertices as an earlier pass (NFL Blitz 2003: jersey
names/numbers and face details over the body, depth test LEQUAL). On hardware both passes produce
identical depth; different WGSL shader variants may not, so the overlay failed the depth test and
vanished. @invariant makes every shader compute the position the same way.

diff --git a/lib/gx/shader.cpp b/lib/gx/shader.cpp
index 2d10095..b9ee354 100644
--- a/lib/gx/shader.cpp
+++ b/lib/gx/shader.cpp
@@ -1990,7 +1990,7 @@ var<storage, read> abuf: array<u32>;
 var<uniform> ubuf: Uniform;{1}
 
 struct VertexOutput {{
-    @builtin(position) pos: vec4f,{2}
+    @builtin(position) @invariant pos: vec4f,{2}
 }};
 
 @vertex
